WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.200
Blackbeard might have a Mythical Zoan fruit&nbsp;
and by the series’ end his powers might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.480
so broken that he can control the seas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:15.920
themselves.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:19.760
Big spoiler warning if you haven’t caught up with&nbsp;
the manga yet, but the last few chapters of One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.760
Piece were a complete game changer and that’s&nbsp;
putting it lightly. Go ahead and click off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.440
video and spend some quality time on VIZ if you’re&nbsp;
not there yet. We’ll see you back here soon!

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:36.640
Today we’re making the bittersweet decision that&nbsp;
it might be time to retire some of our favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:42.080
Blackbeard devil fruit theories from throughout&nbsp;
the years. Goodbye to Cerberus. Goodbye to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:48.080
three brothers. Goodbye, even, to the Kraken.&nbsp;
Because given the big reveal of Luffy’s zoan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:57.040
devil fruit a much more interesting option&nbsp;
has now opened up: That Teach has potentially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:04.640
also has eaten a mythical zoan: the Hito&nbsp;
Hito no Mi - Model “Moon God” … Blank…

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.360
Really the jury’s still out on what Oda&nbsp;
is going to call this one. There’s no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.040
telling what Oda will decide to name&nbsp;
the Moon God of the One Piece world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:19.120
but since Sun God Nika is an original creation&nbsp;
and not directly borrowed from any mythology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:26.480
it’s unlikely we’ll see a Tsukuyomi or Artemis&nbsp;
fruit anytime soon. Instead, Blackbeard’s fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:32.960
will probably also be based on a God unique to&nbsp;
One Piece, merging different cultural ideas.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.280
What’s up, I’m Manu and today we’re talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:47.280
Marshall D. Teach and the secret&nbsp;
identity of the Yami Yami no Mi.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:54.640
I mean, for years and years we’ve theorized about&nbsp;
what Blackbeard’s zoan will be. There are so many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:02:00.560
threes associated with Teach - his three pistols,&nbsp;
the three skulls on his flag, the three claws on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:07.200
the weapon that he used to scar Shanks. Naturally,&nbsp;
he’d have three devil fruits, too - a logia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:13.600
the Yami Yami no Mi - a paramecia, the Gura&nbsp;
Gura no Mi - and a to-be-determined zoan fruit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.480
We thought for sure that this was hinting&nbsp;
toward a Cerberus with its three heads or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:34.400
a Kraken with its three hearts. And&nbsp;
while those are still possibilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.760
we have to welcome a new theory to the club.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.520
So why do we suddenly think that he&nbsp;
actually has a Moon God fruit? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:52.640
because Luffy has the Sun God fruit, of course!

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:58.480
Luffy and Blackbeard have always been opposites.&nbsp;
Throughout the story, they have always paralleled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:05.040
and mirrored one another. If Luffy is the sun, as&nbsp;
you will see, it only makes sense that Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.640
is the moon, the two most common reoccurring&nbsp;
symbols in the story! If you need a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.600
further convincing, though, here are just a few&nbsp;
ways that these two characters counter each other:

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:18.320
First, their powers rival each other perfectly.&nbsp;
Luffy is made of rubber which can insulate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.120
against the earthquakes that Blackbeard can&nbsp;
produce. Even though the quake-quake fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:28.400
is considered the strongest paramecia&nbsp;
with enough power to destroy the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:33.280
Luffy has a built in immunity against it just&nbsp;
like he did with Eneru’s lightning fruit.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.080
And now, if Luffy’s a Sun God which&nbsp;
could explain his strange ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.240
to produce flames, this runs counter to&nbsp;
Blackbeard’s darkness-darkness fruit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.320
Those flames are literally&nbsp;
light against the darkness.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:59.600
It’s not just their powers that are&nbsp;
opposites, though. Their parallels run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:07.760
much deeper than that and are ingrained&nbsp;
in their character traits. Luffy is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:11.520
Warrior of Liberation - he brings&nbsp;
freedom to the people he meets on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:17.840
every island. However, Blackbeard leaves a path&nbsp;
of devastation behind him wherever he goes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:28.320
We first learned about Blackbeard on Drum&nbsp;
Island - he and his crew scared off Wapol&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.520
and his legion of doctors, but also left&nbsp;
the villagers in fear and turmoil. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:39.040
after the Straw Hats visit Drum Island, they&nbsp;
liberate the people from Wapol’s oppressive rule.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.080
They also acquired one bonus&nbsp;
cotton-candy loving reindeer mascot!

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:51.680
We also see Luffy and Blackbeard as opposites&nbsp;
in the ways they attract their crew mates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:57.520
Luffy and Blackbeard both brought freedom to&nbsp;
their crew in a sense. Zoro was literally released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:03.040
from a stockade, Nami from Arlong’s clutches,&nbsp;
and Robin from the likes of Crocodile and later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:09.040
CP9. However, even the Straw Hats that weren’t&nbsp;
freed from literal imprisonment were freed from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:13.920
figurative prison. Usopp, Sanji, and many&nbsp;
others were lifted from their ordinary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:19.920
lives and obligations. Luffy enabled them to&nbsp;
travel the world in pursuit of their dreams.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.240
Luffy gathers his strength from his&nbsp;
crewmates and depends on them, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.600
also allows them to chase their own&nbsp;
goals and find their own sense of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:31.760
fulfillment. On the other hand, Blackbeard&nbsp;
frees many of his crewmates from Impel Down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:37.760
but it’s so they can serve his interests -&nbsp;
not so they can live out their own dreams…

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:41.200
...which for most of the Level 5&nbsp;
prisoners, you know, is probably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:47.840
just murder actually…so maybe Pizarro does&nbsp;
feel a deep sense of fulfillment after all.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:55.680
Even the ways Luffy and Blackbeard&nbsp;
received their fruits are opposites.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:02.000
The Hito Hito no Mi: Model Nika almost seemed to&nbsp;
seek out Luffy specifically. The Gorosei describe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.920
it evading the World Government for 800 years,&nbsp;
as if the fruit has a will of its own. It seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:13.280
like Luffy was chosen by the fruit to carry&nbsp;
on the will of Joyboy and the Sun God Nika.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:19.200
Contrast this with Blackbeard who was on the&nbsp;
hunt for the Yami Yami no Mi and murdered his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:25.440
crewmate Thatch in order to obtain its power.&nbsp;
He also killed Whitebeard in order to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:32.800
his fruit as well. He wasn’t chosen by his&nbsp;
fruit - he sought out his fruit at any cost.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:38.851
Luffy just innocently taking a bit out of Shanks’&nbsp;
treasure just doesn’t give the same vibe as cold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.851 --> 00:06:43.760
blooded killing. I’d go as far as to say&nbsp;
they give off the opposite vibe, actually.

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:54.400
In so many ways, Luffy and Blackbeard&nbsp;
are diametrically opposed. They are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:08.240
direct opposites. Therefore, if Luffy is the sun,&nbsp;
it makes sense that Blackbeard would be the moon.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.720
Obviously, the moon is important to One&nbsp;
Piece as a whole, too. If the Sun God&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:18.000
Nika fruit was foreshadowed even from the&nbsp;
first chapter being titled Romance Dawn and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.440
from other clues like the Straw Hat’s&nbsp;
ship being called the Thousand Sunny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.240
then you’d think there would to be a Moon God&nbsp;
fruit, too with how prominent the moon is overall.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:31.600
Here are just a few of the ways that&nbsp;
the moon features heavily in the series:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:37.200
Eneru’s entire goal was to sail the Arc Maxim up&nbsp;
to the endless land mass that was “Fairy Vearth.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:41.840
And, in Eneru’s cover story we found that not only&nbsp;
are there space pirates kicking it on the moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:47.280
but there are many archaeological clues that&nbsp;
the winged races from the sky islands actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:52.640
originally came from the moon. In the library of&nbsp;
Ohara, we see a planetary model that shows the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:57.840
One Piece world having multiple moons. The minks&nbsp;
transform into their powerful Sulong forms in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.840 --> 00:08:03.520
light of the full moon. And, the surnames of the&nbsp;
Wano clans also contain the Kanji for “moon” for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:17.116
instance, Kozuki means “Light Moon”, Shimotsuki&nbsp;
means “Frost Moon”, and the list just goes on.

00:08:17.116 --> 00:08:19.760
The moon isn’t just important&nbsp;
for One Piece as a whole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:24.640
either. The moon also seems to hold&nbsp;
special significance for Marshall D.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:31.440
Teach himself. When Eiichiro Oda drew Blackbeard&nbsp;
as a child, we see him sitting and crying while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:37.280
a crescent moon hangs in the sky above him.&nbsp;
We also know that Blackbeard never sleeps.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:43.440
I mean, he really needs to try taking melatonin.&nbsp;
His insomnia might be even worse than mine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:50.960
Maybe he, too, is just a coffee lover. Or maybe a&nbsp;
Moon God is naturally active and alert at night?

00:08:52.640 --> 00:08:57.440
We’ve established that due to the parallels&nbsp;
between Blackbeard and Luffy, he probably posesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:05.040
a Moon God devil fruit. However, what exactly does&nbsp;
that mean? What abilities does a Moon God have?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:10.800
In the same way you wouldn’t expect a Sun God to&nbsp;
be made of rubber, what can Blackbeard do with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:16.000
this fruit? Sure, he already has the wildly&nbsp;
strong mastery of earthquakes and darkness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.200
but in the same way Luffy’s new power is broken -&nbsp;
ruled by his imagination and the boundlessness of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:27.600
cartoon logic, what borderline unstoppable powers&nbsp;
should we expect from Blackbeard moving forward?

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:38.880
Many people assume that Blackbeard will acquire&nbsp;
a mythical zoan later on, but I think it’s more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:45.280
likely that, like Luffy, he’s had his mythical&nbsp;
zoan all along. In the same way that what Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:50.880
thought was the Gomu Gomu no Mi was actually the&nbsp;
Hito Hito no Mi: Model Sun God Nika, Blackbeard’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:57.280
darkness darkness fruit might actually the Moon&nbsp;
God fruit. This would play into the opposites once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.280 --> 00:10:02.960
again - Luffy thought he was a paramecia, but was&nbsp;
a zoan. Well, Blackbeard says he’s a logia, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:10.800
is actually a zoan as well. But while Luffy was&nbsp;
totally ignorant of his own fruit and still his,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:18.080
Blackbeard is fully aware but makes other people&nbsp;
ignorant of the true nature of his abilities.

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:22.640
The Yami Yami no Mi actually being the&nbsp;
Hito Hito no Mi: Model Moon God Blank

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:27.680
…wow, we really need Oda to give&nbsp;
us the name so we know what to call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:33.920
it…Anyway, the Yami Yami no Mi actually being&nbsp;
the…Moon God fruit… makes a lot of sense.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:38.720
When Blackbeard fights Ace, Ace actually&nbsp;
comments that Blackbeard’s fruit doesn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.080
“feel” like a logia.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.800
Ace would be something of an expert, too,&nbsp;
wielding the Mera Mera no Mi. It makes sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:55.760
too, because Blackbeard doesn’t turn into&nbsp;
or generate darkness - he’s different from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.760 --> 00:10:58.480
every other logia fruit&nbsp;
user we’ve met in that way.

00:10:58.480 --> 00:11:03.840
Instead, the darkness fruit demonstrates&nbsp;
strange powers. He sucks things in with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:09.280
power closer to gravity than darkness. He can&nbsp;
negate someone else’s devil fruit powers when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:15.600
he makes contact with them. Again, not something&nbsp;
that logically makes sense with darkness. He also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:20.800
amplifies the physical damage that he himself&nbsp;
takes - none of these really make sense for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:28.080
darkness-darkness fruit, but could be explained&nbsp;
by mysterious properties of a Moon God fruit.

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:37.680
It’s similar to how some of Luffy’s powers didn’t&nbsp;
make sense for a rubber fruit - generating flames&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:42.800
with Red Hawk, changing directions with the&nbsp;
jet culverin, even things as basic as Gear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:47.840
2nd and Gear 3rd don’t really make sense&nbsp;
without a heaping helping of anime logic.

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:51.280
But in addition to what Blackbeard can already do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:55.040
just like Luffy’s awakening unlocked&nbsp;
a whole host of new abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.040 --> 00:12:01.840
we’ll probably get some wild new powers once&nbsp;
the truth of Blackbeard’s fruit is revealed.

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:04.480
One of those powers? Hitting the subscribe button.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:08.000
But what else could a Moon God possibly do? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:12.320
we know that Oda takes tons of&nbsp;
inspiration from mythologies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:18.000
around the world. Maybe some of the lunar deities&nbsp;
from across the globe can give us some hints.

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:24.000
The main Egyptian Moon God is Khonsu, but I’ll&nbsp;
leave it to Oscar Isaac to explain that one.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:28.480
However, the Egyptian God Thoth is also&nbsp;
connected to the moon as well as being a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:34.080
God of wisdom and knowledge. And while Blackbeard&nbsp;
certainly possesses a lot of secret knowledge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:40.640
this doesn’t scream “power-up”. The Greek moon&nbsp;
goddesses, such as Artemis, are often associated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:45.840
with the hunt. Again, Blackbeard doesn’t seem&nbsp;
connected to hunting or wild animals, but we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:51.200
do see his crew hunting down powerful devil fruits&nbsp;
like Jesus Burgess did in Dressrosa. Another Greek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:58.000
Moon God, Selene, has power over illusions -&nbsp;
While not Blackbeard himself, his crew mates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:05.840
Shiryu and Catarina Devon use illusory powers&nbsp;
in the form of invisibility and shapeshifting.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:15.200
Across many, many cultures lunar deities are&nbsp;
also connected to childbirth, but I hope for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:19.280
all of our sakes that Blackbeard’s&nbsp;
power is not connected to that because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:23.280
Teach is that last person I want&nbsp;
to see in the maternity ward.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:28.960
Of course, with One Piece being a manga,&nbsp;
we can’t forget about Japanese mythology.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:34.480
In Shinto, the Moon God Tuskuyomi is set&nbsp;
in conflict against the Sun God Amaterasu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:40.960
There’s not much to say about any inspiration&nbsp;
for powers, but it’s worth noting that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:46.880
conflict between these two gods originated from&nbsp;
a fight over food. That reminds me quite a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:51.360
of a certain argument between Luffy and&nbsp;
Blackbeard over some Jayan cherry pies.

00:13:56.800 --> 00:14:01.840
Of course, I am leaving out one of the&nbsp;
obvious powers associated with the moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:05.600
though. One that’s especially&nbsp;
significant given that One Piece is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:09.600
seafaring adventure. The moon’s&nbsp;
gravity controls the tides.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:16.080
Could the same “gravity” of the&nbsp;
darkness-darkness fruit control the sea itself?

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:20.880
I know, I know: It sounds crazy, since&nbsp;
water is a devil fruit user’s weakness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:24.880
but it’s not unheard of for a devil&nbsp;
fruit user to manipulate water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:29.760
indirectly. While they can’t go&nbsp;
for a swim, we do see Aokiji freeze&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:44.320
massive tidal waves at Marineford and Charlotte&nbsp;
Oven boils the sea around Whole Cake Island.

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:49.360
If Blackbeard could influence tides, then&nbsp;
he could easily sink opposing ships and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:55.200
have an advantage in combat over other devil&nbsp;
fruit users. He could also make it extremely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:59.840
difficult to travel to certain islands&nbsp;
- in opposition to Luffy’s liberation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:03.680
he’d be literally restricting&nbsp;
people’s freedom of travel.

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:08.880
Could a previous user of the Moon God fruit&nbsp;
- or even the original Moon God itself - be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.880 --> 00:15:13.920
responsible for phenomena like the calm belt and&nbsp;
the unpredictable weather of the Grand Line? We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:18.640
know that devil fruit awakenings can leave a&nbsp;
lasting impact on the world’s landscape, just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:25.280
like how Aokiji and Akainu changed Punk Hazard’s&nbsp;
environment. It would make total sense if a devil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:31.920
fruit was responsible for the Grand Line itself,&nbsp;
and why not one as powerful as a Moon God fruit?

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:36.080
Since Luffy’s fruit is boundless and&nbsp;
only limited by his own imagination,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:42.320
he needs a foe that has a similar level&nbsp;
of over-poweredness - breaking the taboo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.320 --> 00:15:46.160
between devil fruits and water would&nbsp;
be one way for Blackbeard to achieve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:52.240
a borderline broken ability and make for&nbsp;
a stellar final fight between the two.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:16:00.880
Another possibility, aside from control over the&nbsp;
oceans, could have to do with Blackbeard’s ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:07.840
to consume multiple fruits. This strange power,&nbsp;
exclusive to Blackbeard, has yet to be explained.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:22.320
We know that in Jaya, Luffy and Zoro referred&nbsp;
to Blackbeard as “them” as if he had multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:28.160
identities. Does the Moon God act as its own&nbsp;
entity, separate from Teach? Does it have to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:33.760
with the gravity of pulling things in? Maybe it’s&nbsp;
yet another opposite of Luffy’s abilities: While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:40.400
the Sun God gives freedom and empowers others, the&nbsp;
Moon God is able to take in more power for itself.

00:16:40.400 --> 00:16:45.200
Now this video mostly talked about Blackbeards&nbsp;
powers, but if you really want to understand who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:52.000
Teach really is and why he is so important to the&nbsp;
story, you really shouldn’t ignore this next video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:58.160
here where I explain his entire character and&nbsp;
the three brothers theory as a cherry on top.

